# Audit Report: Ferryx Terminal Output Scheduling, Replay, and Activity Continuity

## 1. Executive Summary & Verification Findings
* **Immediate `terminal.write` Verification**: **YES**. Every incoming IPC chunk currently causes an immediate, synchronous `terminal.write(text)` call on the JS main thread (`ui/src/lib/terminalHostManager.ts:135`, `175`; `ui/src/remote/RemoteTerminal.tsx:137-139`). There is currently no animation-frame batching or write-queue scheduling on the frontend.
* **Inactive-Session Replay Verification**: Replay reaches inactive/reattached renderers via dual buffers:
  1. **Tauri Desktop**: The frontend singleton `TerminalEventBus` maintains an in-memory chunk ring (`SessionBacklog`) per session up to 512 KiB chars (`ui/src/lib/terminalEvents.ts:153-176`). When a renderer is mounted or switched, `subscribeOutput(..., replay = true)` synchronously replays the concatenated backlog into the newly bound `terminal.write` (`ui/src/lib/terminalEvents.ts:98-101`).
  2. **Remote / Daemon**: `TerminalService.attach()` fetches the Rust `BoundedBuffer` snapshot (up to 512 KiB) from `TerminalOutputHub` (`src-tauri/src/terminal/output_hub.rs:72-81`) and sends it as the initial binary frame over WebSocket (`src-tauri/src/remote/server.rs:479-481`).

---

## 2. Pipeline Architecture & Exact Functions

### Backend (Rust / PTY / IPC)
| Component | File & Line | Function / Symbol | Description & Ordering Guarantee |
|---|---|---|---|
| PTY Reader Loop | `src-tauri/src/terminal/session.rs:50-65` | `PtySession::new` | Blocking reader thread reading 4 KiB chunks and sending via `tokio::sync::mpsc::channel(1024)`. Strictly FIFO. |
| Output Pump | `src-tauri/src/terminal/service.rs:56-62` | `TerminalService::spawn_in_worktree` | Async task forwarding PTY receiver chunks into `TerminalOutputHub::publish`. |
| Hub Ring Buffer | `src-tauri/src/terminal/output_hub.rs:20-39`, `60-70` | `BoundedBuffer::push`, `TerminalOutputHub::publish` | Stores chunks in `VecDeque<Vec<u8>>` capped at 512 KiB; evicts oldest chunks from head. Broadcasts to `broadcast::channel(1024)`. |
| IPC Coalescer | `src-tauri/src/ipc/terminal.rs:121-139`, `217-278` | `flush_terminal_output`, `cmd_terminal_spawn` | Coalesces broadcast chunks up to 32 KiB (`BATCH_MAX_BYTES`) or 10ms (`BATCH_FLUSH_INTERVAL`), base64 encodes, and emits Tauri event `terminal_output`. |
| Remote Socket | `src-tauri/src/remote/server.rs:470-496` | `handle_terminal_socket` | Sends initial snapshot history binary frame, then streams live `broadcast_rx` chunks over WebSocket. |

### Frontend (TypeScript / xterm.js / Event Bus)
| Component | File & Line | Function / Symbol | Description & Ordering Guarantee |
|---|---|---|---|
| Stream UTF-8 Decoder | `ui/src/lib/terminalOutput.ts:20-23` | `TerminalOutputDecoderRegistry.decode` | Stateful `TextDecoder("utf-8", { fatal: false })` decoding base64 streaming bytes across IPC chunk boundaries without multi-byte corruption. |
| Event Bus Dispatcher | `ui/src/lib/terminalEvents.ts:135-138`, `145-183` | `TerminalEventBus.handleOutput`, `publishOutput` | Ingests decoded text, scans OSC 0/1/2 titles across chunk carries (`ui/src/lib/terminalEvents.ts:29-53`), updates session backlog buffer, and synchronously invokes registered `outputListeners`. |
| Inactive OSC Scanner | `ui/src/lib/terminalEvents.ts:29-53` | `scanTerminalOscTitles` | Runs on all output regardless of UI mount state; allows background/inactive tabs to update activity titles without an active renderer. |
| Host Manager Binding | `ui/src/lib/terminalHostManager.ts:133-138`, `172-177` | `TerminalHostManager.createInstance`, `updateSession` | Directly connects `terminalEventBus.subscribeOutput` to `terminal.write(text)`. |

